{
  "abstract": "We study the canonical extension of rational symmetric Diophantine quadruples to symmetric sextuples. The construction factors through an explicit genus-one torsor, followed by two further square conditions. For every nonzero reduced parameter $z=M/N$, we prove that the torsor is everywhere locally soluble exactly when $|v_2(z)|\\ge2$ and every prime congruent to three modulo four has even valuation in $M^4+M^2N^2+N^4$. A two-isogeny descent proves that the associated elliptic curves have rank at least one outside the exceptional parameters $z=\\pm1$; a rational torsor point with nonsquare $1+z^2$ forces rank at least two. At $z=8/3$, we prove that the locally soluble torsor has no rational point. Two explicit tangent factorizations constrain an integer's odd part modulo eight, contradicting its value at every 2-adic point. This elementary obstruction requires no elliptic rank computation or saturation certificate. In a complementary fibration fixing one circle coordinate, we prove that the visible boundary subgroup and its complete 2-adic closure cannot satisfy the retained square conditions. Every full rational lift therefore requires rank at least two on an appropriately oriented fiber. We construct an infinite rational family with two independent directions, prove independence through their different 2-adic depths, and exhibit an infinite subfamily satisfying all fifteen edge conditions over the real, 2-adic, and 3-adic fields. Its remaining rational conditions are two explicit genus-four quotient covers, with the additional circle square conditions retained. Exact arithmetic programs accompany the proofs. The results distinguish local solubility, rational source points, and full tuple lifts within this construction; they neither produce a septuple nor exclude arbitrary septuples.",
